package internal

// Generated by a throwaway harness on a research branch that imports
// github.com/jakecoffman/cp/v2 v2.4.0; main's go.mod never gains cp. Each row
// is one tick of cp's own Space.Step over the two-Body scene
// TestEveryJointKindMatchesChipmunkOverAShortHorizon builds, with cp's
// collisionSlop set to the port's 0.005 and ten iterations, and the port run at
// an ErrorBias of -60*ln(0.9) so that its rate reproduces cp's stored 0.9^60
// byte for byte -- collisionBias has no setter, and the Joint's errorBias is
// the same quantity.
//
// The thirteen numbers of a row are A's place, Angle, velocity and Angular
// velocity, then B's, then the Joint's own GetImpulse. cp's a and b are the
// port's B and A, so every constructor in the harness was handed (B, A).
//
// The scenes carry no Shape at all, so there is no Contact anywhere in them.
// That is what makes an exact comparison possible: cp spends its bias velocity
// at the top of the next step's position integration and the port applies it as
// a position delta before Solve returns, which is a one-tick shift -- but only
// Contacts ever write a bias velocity, Joints pushing the Bodies' own.
